  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0 (branch cut from upstream/main 6a10c5ad).\n\n## What changed\n`crates/app/tests/coarse_laws.rs` (test only, no product change): the expected refusal text is now built from `model_fidelity::TOO_COARSE` instead of a hard-coded \"re-import with a larger budget\", so the expectation follows the product wording.\n\n## Cause\n#1064 (#904) added `coarse_laws.rs` expecting \"re-import with a larger budget\". #1074 (#1054) reworded `model_fidelity::TOO_COARSE` to \"re-import with a larger STEP facet budget\" and updated the suites it knew, not this one. Each PR was green alone; main went red on 4 `coarse_laws` tests.\n\nThe other \"larger budget\" hits on main are in `docs/decisions/864-*.md` and `docs/decisions/1054-*.md`; they are historical records and were left as is.\n\n## How tested\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test coarse_laws --test model_fidelity --test step_budget`: coarse_laws 6 passed, model_fidelity 9 passed, step_budget 6 passed, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Pinning test: `coarse_laws` (the refusal expectation in `refusal()`).\n\n## Not exercised\nFull gate tiers (batch/release); other crates untouched.\n\n## Notes\nThe commit's body lacks the Co-Authored-By trailer (the commit was pushed before this was noticed; amending would need a force-push, which is not allowed).\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #1178\n",
